  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The original expression requires \\(a\\ne1.\\) For such \\(a,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} 1+\\frac{a}{1-a} &=\\frac{1-a+a}{1-a}\\\\ &=\\frac1{1-a}. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore the expression is \\(1-(1-a)=a.\\) The restriction \\(a\\ne1\\) remains.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine \\(1+\\frac{a}{1-a}\\) before taking its reciprocal",
        "Retain every restriction imposed by the original denominator"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
